{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Have you anyone else here.</b> If you have sons-in-law:" "<b>and your sons.</b> Or sons-in-law, who are like your sons and your daughters. Now this is an objection against the one who says that one [angel] went to save Lot, for both of them spoke to him, and further, \"for we are about to destroy\" (verse 13). Also the one who spoke with Lot afterward, when he said to him, \"you have magnified your kindness\" (Genesis 19:19)—he said, \"for I cannot do anything\" (Genesis 19:22)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:06.299928982Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}